@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.5.7
@changelog
  - Codename: Say my name.
  - The UF1's soft-key bank names itself: switch it and the name flashes across the time display for about a second, then the clock comes back. On by default, in Settings, Behaviour, UF1.
  - Banks carry a name of your own, one per bank and per modifier set, typed in Settings, Bindings, UF1. The field is never empty: without a name it shows what the bank will announce anyway, and clearing it puts that back.
  - A bank with no name announces what kind of dynamic bank it is (EFFECTS, GROUPS, COLOURS, FAVS) or else its number (SOFT 3).
  - Holding SHIFT counts as a bank switch, because a modifier set is a bank of its own. If that set simply takes Plain's bank, nothing flashes.
  - While you type a bank name the UF1 shows it, so you read the real cells in the real font. Seven segments have no shape for K, M, V, W or X, so Mix Keys arrives as MIH KEYS. With no UF1 attached the editor draws the ten cells instead.
  - The time display's three formats are its own: Time is minutes and seconds, Bars and Samples as before, none of them asking what REAPER's ruler or transport is set to.
  - Negative positions read correctly. With a negative project start time a cursor 26 ms before zero reached the field as -1:59:59:29.
  - Envelope mode: Cmd pulls a time selection wherever the wheel is on the play cursor, which now includes Envelope once its centre key has handed the wheel to the playhead.
  - Envelope mode: once the cursor has moved, the arrows start from where it now is rather than from a point selected before the move.
  - Envelope mode: the centre key's LED shows which of the two targets the wheel is on, in the colours you gave that key. It used to be lit in both.
  - Nav Mode: a marker or region with no name reads Region 3 or Marker 7, on the number REAPER shows in the ruler, instead of arriving as a blank strip.
  - Focused-track panel: two new elements, UF1 encoder mode and UF1 jog mode, both off by default.
  - FX Learn: the page row stopped fighting its own click. The + that starts a new page was dead whenever the UF1 was showing the plug-in being edited. Both editors also move the device onto a page once something is bound there.
  - Three text fields could write onto the wrong object when the thing they belong to changed under the cursor: the bank name, FX Learn's Display label and the UF1 cell's Display name.
  - The MODE-hold menu takes the soft-key highlight with it, so a dynamic bank's selection no longer sits under the mode names.
  - SCRUB is greyed out like MODE. It picks the Jog Mode and never reached the binding system, so an action put there could never fire. Both keys say what they do on hover.
  - The dynamic-bank pager line names both page arrows, not just one.
  - Settings, Modes, NAV lists every key bound to each Nav toggle, by silk-screen label.
  - The UF1's Strip Mode window follows a channel change. Only the UF8's did.
  - The bindings file moves to version 32. The addition is the bank names and nothing else; an older configuration loads unchanged.
